---

## 🚀 Features Breakdown

### 1. Dashboard
- Real-time KPIs (OEE, throughput, utilization)
- Production charts & trends
- Active order status
- Bottleneck alerts

### 2. Production Scheduler
- AI-generated optimal schedule
- Interactive Gantt chart
- Manual override option
- Algorithm comparison (RL vs GA vs Greedy)

### 3. Digital Twin
- SimPy-based factory simulation
- Live machine & worker states
- What-if scenario runner
- Disruption injection (breakdown, delay, priority change)

### 4. Disruption Management
- Auto-detect disruptions
- Generate recovery plans
- Impact analysis

### 5. AI Insights (Gemini)
- Natural language explanations of schedules
- Improvement recommendations
- Chat interface for factory queries

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack Details

### Backend
- **FastAPI** — Modern async web framework
- **SQLAlchemy 2.0** — ORM with type hints
- **Pydantic v2** — Data validation
- **Gymnasium** — RL environment interface
- **Stable-Baselines3** — DQN agent implementation
- **SimPy** — Discrete-event simulation
- **Google Generative AI** — Gemini API SDK

### Frontend
- **React 18** — UI library
- **Vite** — Fast build tool
- **TailwindCSS** — Utility-first styling
- **Recharts** — Chart library
- **Framer Motion** — Animations
- **Lucide React** — Icons
- **Axios** — HTTP client
- **React Router** — Routing

### Database
- **SQLite** — Lightweight, file-based (ideal for practice projects)

---

## ⚙️ Installation & Setup

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.10+
- Node.js 18+
- Git

### Backend Setup

```bash
cd backend

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate (Windows)
venv\Scripts\activate

# Activate (Mac/Linux)
source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Setup environment
copy .env.example .env    # Windows
cp .env.example .env      # Mac/Linux
# Add your GEMINI_API_KEY in .env

# Initialize database
python scripts/init_db.py

# Seed sample data
python scripts/seed_data.py

# Run server
uvicorn main:app --reload
Backend will be live at: http://localhost:8000
Swagger docs at: http://localhost:8000/docs

Frontend Setup
bash
cd frontend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Setup environment
copy .env.example .env    # Windows
cp .env.example .env      # Mac/Linux

# Run dev server
npm run dev
Frontend will be live at: http://localhost:5173

Train RL Agent (Optional)
bash
cd backend
python scripts/train_rl_agent.py
Trained model will be saved in backend/app/ai/rl_agent/saved_models/.

📚 API Endpoints (Preview)
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/products	List all products
POST	/api/products	Create product
GET	/api/machines	List all machines
GET	/api/orders	List all orders
POST	/api/schedule/generate	Generate AI schedule
POST	/api/simulation/run	Run digital twin scenario
POST	/api/disruptions/inject	Simulate disruption
POST	/api/insights/analyze	Get Gemini insights
Full API docs: See docs/API_DOCUMENTATION.md

🧪 Testing
bash
cd backend
pytest tests/ -v
